{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n-th Bell number, which represents the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    It computes the Bell triangle (Aitken's array) iteratively to find the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the first row of the Bell triangle (B(0)), which acts as the 'previous_row'.\n    previous_row = [1]\n\n    # Iterate from r=1 up to n to compute each subsequent row of the triangle.\n    for r in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The current row will have r+1 elements.\n        current_row = [0] * (r + 1)\n\n        # The first element of the current row (T[r][0]) is the last element of the previous row (T[r-1][r-1]).\n        current_row[0] = previous_row[-1]\n\n        # Calculate subsequent elements in the current row using the formula T[r][c] = T[r][c-1] + T[r-1][c-1].\n        for c in range(1, r + 1):\n            current_row[c] = current_row[c-1] + previous_row[c-1]\n\n        # The current_row becomes the previous_row for the next iteration.\n        previous_row = current_row\n\n    # After computing up to row 'n', the first element of that row (previous_row[0]) is B(n).\n    return previous_row[0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if array is monotonic (non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    Handles empty and single-element arrays correctly.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] < array[i - 1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if array[i] > array[i - 1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing"}
