{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(elements: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the Comb Sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_gap(current_gap: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the next gap size using a shrink factor of 1.3.\"\"\"\n        gap = int(current_gap / 1.3)\n        if gap < 1:\n            return 1\n        return gap\n\n    def _perform_swap(elements_list: list, i: int, j: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Swaps elements at specified indices in the list.\"\"\"\n        elements_list[i], elements_list[j] = elements_list[j], elements_list[i]\n\n    n = len(elements)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    result = elements[:]  # Create a shallow copy of the list to avoid modifying the original\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = _calculate_gap(gap)\n        swapped = False\n        \n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if result[i] > result[i + gap]:\n                _perform_swap(result, i, i + gap)\n                swapped = True\n    \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that inputs are list-like structures.\n    Per constraints, this simplified validation always returns True.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _search_contiguous(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs the actual contiguous subsequence search.\n    Iterates through main_list to find a matching slice.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sublist)\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+m] == sublist:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef is_sublist(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given sublist appears as a contiguous subsequence within the main list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_inputs(main_list, sublist):\n        return False\n\n    # An empty sublist is always considered a sublist.\n    if not sublist:\n        return True\n\n    # If sublist is not empty but main_list is, or sublist is longer, it cannot be found.\n    if not main_list or len(sublist) > len(main_list):\n        return False\n\n    return _search_contiguous(main_list, sublist)"}
