{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef find_tuples(tuple_list: List[Tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples where all elements are divisible by k from the given list of tuples.\n    This function validates input and filters the list based on divisibility.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input(input_tuple_list: List[Tuple[int, ...]], divisor: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates input parameters for safety and correctness.\"\"\"\n        if divisor == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"k cannot be zero\")\n\n    def _check_tuple_divisibility(tuple_item: Tuple[int, ...], divisor: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if all elements in a tuple are divisible by divisor.\"\"\"\n        for element in tuple_item:\n            if element % divisor != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _filter_qualifying_tuples(input_tuple_list: List[Tuple[int, ...]], divisor: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n        \"\"\"Filters input list to return only qualifying tuples.\"\"\"\n        filtered_list = []\n        for tup in input_tuple_list:\n            if _check_tuple_divisibility(tup, divisor):\n                filtered_list.append(tup)\n        return filtered_list\n\n    _validate_input(tuple_list, k)\n    return _filter_qualifying_tuples(tuple_list, k)"}
