{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is undulating, meaning it alternates between exactly two different digits and has at least 3 digits.\"\"\"\n\n    def extract_digits(num: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Converts an integer into a list of its individual digits.\"\"\"\n        return [int(d) for d in str(num)]\n\n    def validate_minimum_length(digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the list of digits meets the minimum length requirement of 3.\"\"\"\n        return len(digits) >= 3\n\n    def check_alternating_pattern(digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validates if the digits alternate consistently between two distinct values.\"\"\"\n        first_digit = digits[0]\n        second_digit = digits[1]\n\n        if first_digit == second_digit:\n            return False  # Must alternate between *two different* digits\n\n        for i in range(2, len(digits)):\n            if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index positions (0-indexed) should match first_digit\n                if digits[i] != first_digit:\n                    return False\n            else:  # Odd index positions should match second_digit\n                if digits[i] != second_digit:\n                    return False\n        return True\n\n    digits = extract_digits(number)\n\n    if not validate_minimum_length(digits):\n        return False\n\n    return check_alternating_pattern(digits)"}
