{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of times a rotated binary string converts to an odd decimal value.\n    Performs left rotations on the binary string and checks the parity of each resulting decimal.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotations):\n        # Perform a left rotation\n        current_string = current_string[1:] + current_string[0]\n\n        # Convert the rotated string to its decimal equivalent\n        decimal_value = int(current_string, 2)\n\n        # Check if the decimal value is odd\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return odd_count"}
