{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(array: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element that appears only once in a sorted array where other elements appear twice.\n    Uses a binary search approach to efficiently locate the unique element.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n        # Adjust mid to be even if it's currently odd, to ensure pairs start at even indices\n        # This simplifies checking array[mid] and array[mid+1]\n        if mid % 2 == 1:\n            mid -= 1\n\n        # If the elements at mid and mid+1 are the same, it means all elements\n        # before this point are in pairs, so the unique element is to the right.\n        if array[mid] == array[mid+1]:\n            low = mid + 2\n        # Otherwise, the unique element is at or before mid (or at mid itself).\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    \n    # When low == high, this index points to the unique element.\n    return array[low]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def _is_digit(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Returns True if character is a digit 0-9.\"\"\"\n    return '0' <= char <= '9'\n\ndef _validate_empty_or_whitespace(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Returns True if string is empty or contains only whitespace.\"\"\"\n    return not s or s.isspace()\n\ndef _validate_sign_and_digits(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Returns True if string has valid sign and all remaining chars are digits.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    start_idx = 0\n    if s[0] == '-' or s[0] == '+':\n        start_idx = 1\n\n    # Ensure there's at least one digit after the optional sign\n    if start_idx == n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(start_idx, n):\n        if not _is_digit(s[i]):\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef check_integer(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a string represents a valid integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if _validate_empty_or_whitespace(input_string):\n        return False\n    return _validate_sign_and_digits(input_string)"}
