{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def find_first_occurrence(array: list[int], element: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef find_last_occurrence(array: list[int], element: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = find_first_occurrence(array, element, n)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = find_last_occurrence(array, element, n)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
