{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(input_list: list, n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the input parameters for the larg_nnum function.\n    Checks if n is positive and not greater than the list's length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 < n <= len(input_list)):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _sort_descending(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a copy of the input list in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n\ndef _select_top_n(sorted_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Selects the first n items from a sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sorted_list[:n]\n\ndef larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list.\n    The function utilizes helper functions for validation, sorting, and selection.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_inputs(input_list, n):\n        return []\n\n    sorted_list = _sort_descending(input_list)\n    result = _select_top_n(sorted_list, n)\n    return result"}
