{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    # dp_inc[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[i]\n    dp_inc = [0] * n\n    # dp_dec[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at array[i]\n    dp_dec = [0] * n\n\n    # Calculate dp_inc\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp_inc[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                dp_inc[i] = max(dp_inc[i], dp_inc[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Calculate dp_dec\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        dp_dec[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                dp_dec[i] = max(dp_dec[i], dp_dec[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence\n    # A bitonic subsequence with array[i] as the peak has sum dp_inc[i] + dp_dec[i] - array[i]\n    # We initialize max_bitonic_sum with negative infinity to handle arrays with all negative numbers.\n    max_bitonic_sum = -float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = dp_inc[i] + dp_dec[i] - array[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union, Tuple\n\ndef convert(z: Union[complex, float, int]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert complex number to polar coordinates.\n    Returns (magnitude, angle) in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(z, complex):\n        z = complex(z)\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(z.real**2 + z.imag**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
