{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division of two tuples, returning a new tuple with integer results\n    when division produces whole numbers. Assumes valid, equal-length input tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        # Perform division and ensure integer result if it's a whole number\n        division_result = tuple1[i] / tuple2[i]\n        if division_result == int(division_result):\n            result.append(int(division_result))\n        else:\n            result.append(division_result)\n    return tuple(result)"}
