{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def _validate_input(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input n is a positive integer.\n    Returns True if n is positive, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return n > 0\n\ndef _generate_odd_numbers(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Generates a list of the first n odd natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    return [2 * i + 1 for i in range(n)]\n\ndef _calculate_squares(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the square of each number in a given list.\"\"\"\n    return [num ** 2 for num in numbers]\n\ndef square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    Returns 0 if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(n):\n        return 0\n\n    odd_numbers = _generate_odd_numbers(n)\n    squared_numbers = _calculate_squares(odd_numbers)\n    return sum(squared_numbers)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists based on a cyclic pattern.\n    Each element input_list[i] is placed into sublist i % n.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize n empty sublists\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Distribute elements cyclically\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        sublist_index = i % n\n        result[sublist_index].append(item)\n\n    return result"}
