{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array, k, expected_result):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array formed by repeating\n    the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def kadane(arr):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the maximum subarray sum for a given array using Kadane's algorithm.\n        Returns 0 for an empty array, and handles all-negative arrays correctly.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not arr:\n            return 0\n        \n        max_so_far = arr[0]\n        current_max = arr[0]\n        \n        for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n            current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n            \n        return max_so_far\n\n    if not array or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the maximum subarray sum for a single instance of the array.\n    single_pass_max_sum = kadane(array)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return single_pass_max_sum\n\n    # Calculate the total sum of the original array.\n    total_sum_array = sum(array)\n\n    # Form an array by repeating the original array twice to capture sums\n    # that span across the boundary of two blocks.\n    repeated_array_two_blocks = array + array\n    max_sum_two_blocks = kadane(repeated_array_two_blocks)\n\n    if total_sum_array <= 0:\n        # If the total sum of the array is non-positive, repeating the array\n        # more than twice will not increase the maximum sum beyond what's found\n        # in the first two blocks.\n        return max_sum_two_blocks\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is positive, and k > 2, we can enhance the maximum sum\n        # by adding (k - 2) full repetitions of the array.\n        return max_sum_two_blocks + (k - 2) * total_sum_array"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of inversions in an array using a nested loop approach.\n    An inversion is a pair (i,j) where i < j but array[i] > array[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    inv_count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                inv_count += 1\n    return inv_count"}
