{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list, length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from a prefix until index i,\n    mandatorily including the element at index k (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j]\n    # considering elements only up to index i (inclusive).\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Calculate dp values for the prefix arr[0...i]\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j]  # Initialize with the element itself\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[j] > arr[prev]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[prev] + arr[j])\n\n    # Now, find the maximum sum from dp[j] (where j <= i) such that arr[j] < arr[k]\n    # This value will be added to arr[k] to form the total sum.\n    # Initialize to 0, representing an empty prefix subsequence if no element satisfies the condition.\n    max_prefix_sum_before_k = 0\n\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_prefix_sum_before_k = max(max_prefix_sum_before_k, dp[j])\n\n    # The total maximum sum is the best prefix sum found plus the required kth element.\n    return max_prefix_sum_before_k + arr[k]"}
