{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def _find_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the position (0-indexed from the right) of the first unset bit\n    encountered when scanning leftwards from the rightmost set bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    pos_rightmost_set = 0\n    temp_num = number\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        if (temp_num & 1) == 1:\n            break\n        pos_rightmost_set += 1\n        temp_num >>= 1\n\n    current_pos = pos_rightmost_set\n    while True:\n        if not ((number >> current_pos) & 1):\n            return current_pos\n        current_pos += 1\n\ndef _set_bit_at_position(number: int, position: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the bit at the specified position (0-indexed) in the given number.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number | (1 << position)\n\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer, according to the\n    interpretation derived from the example assert statement.\n    \"\"\"\n    position_to_set = _find_left_most_unset_bit(number)\n    return _set_bit_at_position(number, position_to_set)"}
