{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def _generate_gap_sequence(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a gap sequence for Shell Sort, consistent with the provided design context.\n    For n=10, this specifically aims to produce [4, 2, 1].\n    \"\"\"\n    gaps = []\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    # Inferring from the sequence diagram (n=10 -> [4, 2, 1]),\n    # the initial gap appears to be derived from n (e.g., int(n / 2.2)).\n    # Ensure the initial gap is at least 1.\n    gap = max(1, int(n / 2.2)) \n    \n    while gap >= 1:\n        gaps.append(gap)\n        gap //= 2\n    return gaps\n\ndef _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr: list[int], gap: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an insertion sort on elements separated by 'gap' within the array.\n    Elements are shifted to their correct position within their gap-sublist.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(gap, n):\n        temp = arr[i]\n        j = i\n        # Shift elements greater than temp to the right by 'gap' positions\n        while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n            arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n            j -= gap\n        arr[j] = temp\n\ndef shell_sort(array: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array using the Shell Sort algorithm by repeatedly performing\n    gap-based insertion sort with a decreasing sequence of gaps.\n    It returns a new sorted list without modifying the original input array.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    # Handle edge cases: empty or single-element arrays\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(array) # Return a copy for consistency\n\n    # Create a mutable copy of the input array to avoid modifying the original\n    arr = list(array)\n\n    # Generate the sequence of gaps for the Shell Sort\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    # Apply insertion sort for each gap in the sequence\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr, gap)\n\n    return arr"}
