{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "def find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its positions in a given sentence.\n    Returns a tuple (start_position, end_position, adverb_text).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper for input validation\n    def validate_input(sentence_input: str) -> bool:\n        return isinstance(sentence_input, str)\n\n    # Helper for cleaning punctuation\n    def clean_punctuation(word: str) -> str:\n        return ''.join(char for char in word if char.isalnum())\n\n    # Helper for adverb detection\n    def get_adverb_patterns() -> list:\n        # Simple suffix-based adverb detection, could be expanded\n        return [\"ly\", \"ward\", \"wards\", \"wise\"]\n\n    def is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n        cleaned_word = clean_punctuation(word).lower()\n        if not cleaned_word:\n            return False\n        # Heuristic: check common adverb suffixes\n        patterns = get_adverb_patterns()\n        for pattern in patterns:\n            if cleaned_word.endswith(pattern):\n                return True\n        # Add a few common adverbs that might not end in -ly\n        common_adverbs = [\"here\", \"there\", \"now\", \"then\", \"well\", \"fast\", \"always\", \"never\", \"often\", \"seldom\", \"sometimes\", \"today\", \"tomorrow\", \"yesterday\", \"everywhere\", \"somewhere\", \"anywhere\", \"nowhere\", \"soon\", \"late\", \"early\", \"already\", \"almost\", \"just\", \"quite\", \"rather\", \"very\", \"too\", \"enough\", \"hard\", \"much\"]\n        return cleaned_word in common_adverbs\n\n    # Helper for tokenization\n    def tokenize_sentence(sentence_input: str) -> list:\n        return sentence_input.split()\n\n    # Helper for identifying the first adverb\n    def identify_first_adverb(words: list) -> tuple:\n        for i, word in enumerate(words):\n            if is_adverb(word):\n                return i, clean_punctuation(word)\n        return -1, \"\"\n\n    # Helper for calculating positions\n    def calculate_positions(original_sentence: str, word_index: int, adverb: str) -> tuple:\n        words = tokenize_sentence(original_sentence)\n        current_pos = 0\n        for i, word in enumerate(words):\n            if i == word_index:\n                # Find the start index of the raw word in the sentence\n                start_raw = original_sentence.find(word, current_pos)\n                if start_raw == -1: # Should not happen if word is in sentence\n                    return -1, -1\n\n                # Calculate start and end position of the cleaned adverb within the original raw word\n                # This accounts for leading/trailing punctuation in the raw word token\n                clean_adverb_text = clean_punctuation(word)\n                if clean_adverb_text == adverb: # Ensure we are finding the correct cleaned word\n                    start_pos = start_raw + word.find(clean_adverb_text)\n                    end_pos = start_pos + len(clean_adverb_text)\n                    return start_pos, end_pos\n                else:\n                    return -1, -1 # Mismatch after cleaning, should not happen with identify_first_adverb\n            current_pos = original_sentence.find(word, current_pos) + len(word) + 1 # +1 for space\n\n        return -1, -1\n\n    # Helper for creating result tuple\n    def create_result_tuple(start_pos: int, end_pos: int, adverb_text: str) -> tuple:\n        return (start_pos, end_pos, adverb_text)\n\n    if not validate_input(sentence):\n        return (-1, -1, \"\")\n\n    words = tokenize_sentence(sentence)\n    adverb_index, adverb_text = identify_first_adverb(words)\n\n    if adverb_index == -1:\n        return (-1, -1, \"\")\n\n    start_pos, end_pos = calculate_positions(sentence, adverb_index, adverb_text)\n\n    if start_pos == -1:\n        return (-1, -1, \"\")\n\n    return create_result_tuple(start_pos, end_pos, adverb_text)"}
