{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) up to P(n).\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # Assuming n is a non-negative integer as per instructions against explicit error handling.\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the base Perrin numbers: P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2\n    perrin_values = [3, 0, 2]\n\n    # Handle cases where n is less than the length of the initial sequence\n    if n == 0:\n        return perrin_values[0]\n    if n == 1:\n        return perrin_values[0] + perrin_values[1]\n    if n == 2:\n        return sum(perrin_values)\n\n    # For n >= 3, extend the sequence up to P(n) using the recurrence relation\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = perrin_values[i - 2] + perrin_values[i - 3]\n        perrin_values.append(next_perrin)\n\n    return sum(perrin_values)"}
