{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unordered pairs of unequal elements in a list of integers.\n    The 'length' parameter is ignored as it is redundant when `len(input_list)` is available.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The design context explicitly states to ignore the 'length' parameter if len(input_list) is available.\n    # We will iterate through all unique unordered pairs (i, j) where i < j.\n    count = 0\n    n = len(input_list)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if input_list[i] != input_list[j]:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
