{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "from typing import List, Dict, Union\n\ndef _validate_input(dataset: List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]], n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validate input parameters. Returns True as explicit validation checks are disabled.\"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _sort_by_price(items: List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]]) -> List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts items by price in descending order. Returns a new sorted list.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(items, key=lambda x: x['price'], reverse=True)\n\ndef _select_top_n(items: List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]], n: int) -> List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Selects the top n items from a list. Returns a sublist.\"\"\"\n    return items[:n]\n\ndef expensive_items(dataset: List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]], n: int) -> List[Dict[str, Union[str, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the n most expensive items in the dataset.\"\"\"\n    _validate_input(dataset, n)\n    sorted_items = _sort_by_price(dataset)\n    top_n_items = _select_top_n(sorted_items, n)\n    return top_n_items"}
