{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def is_sorted(lst: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if list is sorted in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    return all(lst[i] <= lst[i + 1] for i in range(len(lst) - 1))\n\ndef validate_input(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validate input parameters.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list1, list) or not isinstance(list2, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs list1 and list2 must be lists.\")\n    if not isinstance(size, int) or size < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input size must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if len(list1) != size or len(list2) != size:\n        raise ValueError(\"List lengths must match the provided size.\")\n    if not is_sorted(list1) or not is_sorted(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both lists must be sorted in ascending order.\")\n    return True\n\ndef find_kth_element(list1: list, list2: list, k: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Find kth smallest element in two sorted arrays using binary search.\"\"\"\n    m, n = len(list1), len(list2)\n\n    # Ensure list1 is the shorter array for optimization.\n    if m > n:\n        return find_kth_element(list2, list1, k)\n\n    # Base cases for recursion.\n    if m == 0:\n        return float(list2[k - 1])\n    if k == 1:\n        return float(min(list1[0], list2[0]))\n\n    # Calculate split points for binary search.\n    # i is the number of elements to consider from list1, j from list2.\n    i = min(m, k // 2)\n    j = k - i\n\n    if list1[i - 1] < list2[j - 1]:\n        # If the i-th element of list1 is smaller, discard list1[:i].\n        return find_kth_element(list1[i:], list2, k - i)\n    elif list1[i - 1] > list2[j - 1]:\n        # If the j-th element of list2 is smaller, discard list2[:j].\n        return find_kth_element(list1, list2[j:], k - j)\n    else:\n        # If they are equal, this element is the k-th smallest.\n        return float(list1[i - 1])\n\ndef get_median(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find median of two sorted lists of same size.\n    Raises ValueError if input validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_input(list1, list2, size)\n\n    # Total elements are 2 * size. Since this is always even,\n    # the median is the average of the (size)-th and (size + 1)-th smallest elements.\n    \n    # Find the (size)-th smallest element.\n    kth_element_1 = find_kth_element(list1, list2, size)\n    \n    # Find the (size + 1)-th smallest element.\n    kth_element_2 = find_kth_element(list1, list2, size + 1)\n    \n    return (kth_element_1 + kth_element_2) / 2.0"}
