{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Returns the calculated area or None if radius is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_radius(radius: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validate that radius is non-negative.\n        Returns True if radius >= 0, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        return radius >= 0\n\n    def _calculate_area(radius: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate triangle area using the formula: area = radius\u00b2.\n        Returns the calculated area.\n        \"\"\"\n        return radius * radius\n\n    if not _validate_radius(radius):\n        return None\n    else:\n        return _calculate_area(radius)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates of the given coordinate tuple, including diagonals.\n    Returns the coordinates in row-major order as a list of lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    center_x, center_y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for x_offset in range(-1, 2):\n        for y_offset in range(-1, 2):\n            adjacent_coords.append([center_x + x_offset, center_y + y_offset])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
