{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all zeroes to the end of the given list while preserving the relative order of non-zero elements.\n    Returns a new list with zeroes moved to the end.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_zero_elements = []\n    zero_count = 0\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        if element != 0:\n            non_zero_elements.append(element)\n        else:\n            zero_count += 1\n\n    # Append all counted zeros to the end of the non-zero elements\n    non_zero_elements.extend([0] * zero_count)\n\n    return non_zero_elements"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list, count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of XOR of all unique pairs of numbers in the given list.\n    Assumes `count` is the length of the `numbers` list.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(count):\n        for j in range(i + 1, count):\n            total_xor_sum += numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n    return total_xor_sum"}
