{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "def is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if string is a decimal number with a precision of 2.\n    It expects a format like 'digits.dd' where digits is one or more numeric characters.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Check for exactly one decimal point\n    if input_string.count('.') != 1:\n        return False\n\n    parts = input_string.split('.')\n    integer_part = parts[0]\n    decimal_part = parts[1]\n\n    # Validate the integer part: must be non-empty and contain only digits\n    if not integer_part or not integer_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    # Validate the decimal part: must have exactly 2 digits and contain only digits\n    if len(decimal_part) != 2 or not decimal_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
