{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "solution": "def test_three_equal(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of equal numbers among three given integers.\n    Returns 3 if all are equal, 2 if exactly two are equal, and 1 if none are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == b and b == c:\n        return 3\n    elif a == b or a == c or b == c:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "import math\n\ndef is_perfect_square(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is a perfect square.\n    A number is a perfect square if its square root is an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    \n    sqrt_number = math.sqrt(number)\n    return sqrt_number == int(sqrt_number)"}
